WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.268
The headline result is that G2N2 does not just
match the theory,

00:00:04.348 --> 00:00:05.967
it dominates in practice.

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:08.617
On QM9, learning targets one at a time,

00:00:08.697 --> 00:00:13.985
it posts the best error on every single target
while training faster than PPGN.

00:00:14.065 --> 00:00:16.770
On the notoriously hard R-squared target,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.828
its error drops to zero-point-three-four-two,

00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:25.060
where PPGN sits at three-point-seven-eight, more
than a ten-fold improvement,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.884
and when all twelve targets are learned at once the
gap widens further.

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:35.931
On graph classification it beats the second-best
network on five of the six TUD datasets.

00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:40.823
And on the spectral test it cleanly learns
band-pass filters where PPGN,

00:00:40.903 --> 00:00:44.560
starved of the memory it would need, essentially fails.
